lauderdale-county"],["ARC or PLC in Lauderdale County","/arc-plc/alabama/lauderdale-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 11 grids April to May came in under 90% of normal in 30 of those years, the fewest of any pair. In 2025 the middle saw May to June at 161% of normal and November to December at 48%. So far in 2026 February to March sits at 51% on the middle. Every grid had its driest year in 2007, with grid 17872 down to 58% that year.</p>"}
